    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main 4cab68f97: a_turning_arc_is_refused_by_name passes without a change. Suggest closing; the maintainer decides.\n\nThe test posts an arc that turns A. It asserts the exact refusal message and checks that no G2 or G3 block is posted. The run passed: 1 passed, 0 failed.\n\nCommand: cargo test -p camcraft-post --test tormach_turning_a_refusals a_turning_arc_is_refused_by_name -- --exact\n\nThis confirms the existing refusal only. The issue asks for missing regression coverage, rather than a behavior fix. That coverage request remains unfinished. The worker instructions require a failing pin before continuing, and require stopping when the pin passes unchanged. I stopped at Step 5. No production code changed. No PR was opened.\n\nThe candidate test remains uncommitted in .claude/worktrees/issue-2470/crates/post/tests/tormach_turning_a_refusals.rs on branch issue/2470-turning-a-refusals. The run output is /tmp/2470-reproduction.log. Claim released.\n",
